# The field starts at 0 and is only ever counted up, so its slot holds an integer. One test of a byte of the cell asks whether the fields are still in their slots.
# Then the likely path is a load, an addition of integers, a store and one test of the range. No double is made and nothing is called.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="hit" role=Source
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#0:
# CHECK-NEXT: Int64 b@[[counter]] = ArgumentReg(
# CHECK-NEXT: Int32 b@[[flags]] = Load8Z(b@[[counter]], offset = 6, ControlDependent|Reads:JSCell_typeInfoFlags, {{*}}:HasBirthFieldsFilled)
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[moved]] = BitAnd(b@[[flags]],
# CHECK: Branch(b@[[moved]], Terminal,
# CHECK-NEXT: Successors: Then:Rare:#{{*}}, Else:#[[count]]
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#[[count]]:
# CHECK-NEXT: Predecessors:
# CHECK-NEXT: b@[[old]] = Load(b@[[counter]], offset = 16, ControlDependent|Reads:ObjectFields
# CHECK-NOT: IToD(
# CHECK-NOT: Patchpoint(
# CHECK: b@[[new]] = Add(b@[[old]],
# CHECK-NOT: IToD(
# CHECK-NOT: Patchpoint(
# CHECK: Store(b@[[new]], b@[[counter]], offset = 16, ControlDependent|Writes:ObjectFields
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# x86-64 adds to the low half of the slot in memory and tests the carry. ARM64 loads, adds, compares and stores.
# X64-LABEL: name="hit" role=Source
# X64-NEXT: instructions: 4, patchpoints: 0
# ARM64-LABEL: name="hit" role=Source
# ARM64-NEXT: instructions: 10, patchpoints: 0
